Feature: What a team believes about the enemy
  A team sees an enemy drone only near its own drones, its towers and its base. For the rest of the
  time it has the place where it last saw the drone, and a guess. The guess is a cloud of
  possible places. A drone that the team does not see flies on to a tower, as an enemy drone
  does, and the cloud spreads out. The cloud has the same chance in each of its places, so a
  commander can ask how likely it is that an enemy drone is near a tower.

  A place that the team looks at, and sees no drone in, is not a place for the drone. The
  guesses that were in the place go. Thus the team can tell where a drone is not.

  Expectation: A drone that the team sees is where the team sees it
    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    Then the spread of the Blue belief of the Red scout is at most 20 m

  Expectation: The team is less sure of a drone that it cannot see
    Overrides: A drone that the team sees is where the team sees it
    The Red scout flies away from the Blue drone. The Blue drone does not see it for 10 s.

    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    When the Red scout flies into the fog for 10 seconds
    Then the spread of the Blue belief of the Red scout is at least 40 m

  Expectation: Where the team looks and sees no drone, the drone is not believed to be
    Overrides: The team is less sure of a drone that it cannot see
    The first Blue drone looks 150 m round it. It does not see the Red scout, so the Red scout
    is not there.

    Given the Red scout is near a Blue drone
    When the Red scout flies into the fog for 10 seconds
    Then the chance on the Blue belief of the Red scout near the first Blue drone is at most 5 %
